WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Since infants are so much smaller than adults or even older children, our chest compressions technique has to adapt to their size while still being powerful enough to move blood to the brain.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:20.000
There are two primary ways to perform infant compressions, the one-handed technique and the two-thumb encircling method.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Depending on the situation and your own comfort, you can choose the one that works best for you.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Your instructor will demonstrate each technique, then give you a chance to practice.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Before beginning compressions, ensure the infant is on a hard, flat surface, such as a sturdy table or even the ground.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:46.000
If they are on a soft crib mattress or a changing pad, your compressions will just push them into the padding instead of squeezing the heart.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.000
You need that solid resistance underneath them to make every push count.

